Hello,

So far, all the Buildroot Developers Meeting have been organized in
Europe: co-located with the FOSDEM in Brussels (Belgium), and
co-located with ELCE (various locations in Europe).

Another major event is the Embedded Linux Conference, for which the
next edition will take place on April 29 - May 1 in San Jose,
California
(http://events.linuxfoundation.org/events/embedded-linux-conference).

Through this e-mail, I'd like to see if there are people interested in
having a Buildroot related meeting co-located with the Embedded Linux
Conference. It might be a Buildroot hacking session, or a day with
Buildroot tutorials, etc.

Is there some interest in this?

Thanks for your feedback,

